{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff\/number"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"title":"number","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLHammerOnPullOffV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"abstract":[{"text":"Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhammeronpulloff\/number"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHammerOnPullOff/number":{"type":"topic","title":"number","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhammeronpulloff\/number","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff\/number","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHammerOnPullOff":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLHammerOnPullOff","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLHammerOnPullOff"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhammeronpulloff","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHammerOnPullOff","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLHammerOnPullOff"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The hammer-on and pull-off elements are used in guitar and fretted instrument notation. Since a single slur","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be marked over many notes, the hammer-on and pull-off elements are separate so the individual pair of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notes can be specified. The element content can be used to specify how the hammer-on or pull-off should be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notated. An empty element leaves this choice up to the application.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}